.TH CBMAP_GET_PTR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cbmap_get_ptr \- get pointer to value by key (type-safe)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cbstmap.h>

value_ptr = cbmap_get_ptr(hm_name, key);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-safe wrapper for cbmap_get_elem_ref() that returns a pointer to the
value, or NULL if key not found. Unlike cbmap_get(), does not terminate
on key_not_found.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
hm_name  BST map to search
key      Key to look up
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns pointer to value if key found
Returns NULL if key not found
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Returns NULL if key not found (does not terminate)
Terminates program if value size doesn't match type size
Returns pointer to value for in-place modification
Pointer invalidated by insert/delete operations
For strings, returns pointer to the char* itself
O(log n) search time
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_get (3),
.BR cbmap_get_elem_ref (3)
